STEVE sketch solver (solver/, web/src/sketch/solver/steve-sketch.{mjs,wasm})
===========================================================================

This component bundles and links the following third-party code.

1. planegcs -- FreeCAD's 2D geometric constraint solver
   License:   GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version
              (per the file headers); STEVE uses it under LGPL-2.1, full text in
              vendor/planegcs/LICENSE.
   Copyright: (c) 2011 Konstantinos Poulios and the FreeCAD contributors (see file headers).
   Upstream:  https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD, directory src/Mod/Sketcher/App/planegcs at
              commit 5f8eac49f31626354ee69bf40616bac801ca5560, plus FreeCAD src/FCConfig.h,
              src/FCGlobal.h, src/boost_graph_adjacency_list.hpp.
   Obtained via the snapshot and patch set of https://github.com/Salusoft89/planegcs
              (npm @salusoft89/planegcs 1.2.0), commit ee9b156da9827a91a56a888a53520f63d5cffaa6
              (2026-07-06), LGPL-2.1 (Copyright (C) 2023 Miroslav Sery, Salusoft89).

   Modifications relative to FreeCAD 5f8eac49 (each modified file carries a header notice):
   a. By Salusoft89/planegcs (update_freecad.sh):
      - GCS.cpp: Base::Console -> Console (local header); "#define BOOST_NO_CXX98_FUNCTION_BASE";
        the dependent-parameter QR runs synchronously instead of via std::async (no threads in
        WebAssembly); System::solve(VEC_pD&, ...) passes its algorithm to initSolution().
      - Constraints.h, GCS.h, Geo.h: removed SketcherGlobal.h include and the SketcherExport macro.
      - headers/FCConfig.h: OS detection accepts "unix"; headers/FCGlobal.h: removed QtCore.h.
   b. By STEVE (2026-09-30):
      - headers/Console.h: rewritten as a portable no-op logger (was Emscripten-only).
      - headers/FCConfig.h: OS detection also accepts __unix__ and __EMSCRIPTEN__.
      - GCS.h: new public System::rebaseReference() (re-bases the reference configuration on the
        current parameters; used for incremental dragging).
      - GCS.cpp, System::identifyDependentParameters(): skips the Gauss-Jordan elimination of R
        when it has full column rank (nothing is read from it then; it cost O(n^3)).
      - GCS.cpp, System::solve(): redundant constraints are checked against the solution (they
        were checked against the pre-solve reference values, so sketches with redundant
        constraints never reported success).
      - Constraints.cpp, ConstraintPointOnBSpline::grad(): updates the knot span like error()
        does (a Jacobian evaluated before the residual used a stale span).
      - qp_eq.cpp: evaluates H * (Y * c) instead of (H * Y) * c (same value, O(n^2) instead of
        O(n^2 m); it dominated the cost of drag frames).
   Unmodified: Geo.cpp, SubSystem.cpp, SubSystem.h, qp_eq.h, Util.h,
   headers/boost_graph_adjacency_list.hpp.

2. nlohmann/json 3.12.0 (vendor/nlohmann/json.hpp)
   License:   MIT, vendor/nlohmann/LICENSE.MIT. Copyright (c) 2013-2025 Niels Lohmann.
   Upstream:  https://github.com/nlohmann/json/releases/download/v3.12.0/json.hpp
              (sha256 aaf127c04cb31c406e5b04a63f1ae89369fccde6d8fa7cdda1ed4f32dfc5de63), unmodified.

3. musl libc 1.2.6, libm subset (vendor/musl-math): sin, cos, sincos, atan, atan2, pow and their
   kernels/tables, compiled into both builds so the results are bit-identical (glibc's versions
   differ from musl's in the last bit).
   License:   MIT, vendor/musl-math/COPYRIGHT. Copyright (c) 2005-2020 Rich Felker et al.; the
              kernels derive from FreeBSD msun (Sun Microsystems, permissive notices in the files)
              and pow/exp data from ARM Limited (MIT).
   Upstream:  copied from Emscripten 6.0.10's bundled musl (system/lib/libc/musl, v1.2.6);
              checksums of the unmodified files in vendor/musl-math/SHA256SUMS.upstream.
   Modified:  libm.h renames the internal kernels __sin/__cos/__tan(l) to __steve_musl_* (they
              clash with glibc's <math.h> declarations). Added shims: features.h (defines `hidden`
              on top of the platform header), fp_arch.h (generic, empty).

4. Build-time only, not vendored (header-only, compiled into the binaries):
   Eigen 3.4.0 (MPL-2.0; some optional parts LGPL) -- Debian/Ubuntu package libeigen3-dev.
   Boost Graph headers (Boost Software License 1.0) -- package libboost-dev.
